    "repo": "swesmith/marshmallow-code__webargs.dbde72fe",
    "problem_statement": "# BottleParser doesn't handle invalid JSON properly\n\nI noticed that when sending invalid JSON to a Bottle application using webargs, the application crashes instead of handling the error gracefully.\n\n## Description\n\nThe BottleParser class in `bottleparser.py` seems to be missing error handling for invalid JSON. When a request with malformed JSON is sent to a Bottle application using webargs, it throws an unhandled exception instead of properly handling the error.\n\nThis happens because the code is not catching the `bottle.HTTPError` exception that is raised when invalid JSON is encountered. The application should handle this case gracefully, similar to how other parsers in the library do.\n\n## Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a simple Bottle application using webargs\n2. Send a request with invalid JSON (e.g., malformed JSON or non-UTF8 characters)\n3. Observe that the application crashes with an unhandled exception\n\nExample reproduction code:\n```python\nfrom bottle import Bottle, request, response, run\nfrom webargs import fields\nfrom webargs.bottleparser import use_args\n\napp = Bottle()\n\n@app.route('/echo', method=['POST'])\n@use_args({\"name\": fields.Str(required=True)})\ndef echo(args):\n    return {\"name\": args[\"name\"]}\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    run(app, host='localhost', port=8080)\n```\n\nWhen sending a request with invalid JSON:\n```\ncurl -X POST http://localhost:8080/echo -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d \"{invalid json\"\n```\n\nThe application crashes instead of returning a proper error response.\n\nI think this is a regression as other parsers in the library seem to handle this case properly."
  }
